/-!
# `Tor` of a quotient by a Koszul-regular sequence against a module it kills

Let `R` be a commutative ring and let `f₁, …, f_r ∈ R` be a Koszul-regular sequence (for instance
a regular sequence, by [Stacks, Tag 062F]), with `I = (f₁, …, f_r)`. The Koszul complex
`K_•(f)` is a free resolution of `R ⧸ I`, so `Tor_n^R(R ⧸ I, M)` is the homology of
`K_•(f) ⊗_R M`. If `I` annihilates `M`, every coefficient of the Koszul differential acts as zero
on `M`, the differentials of `K_•(f) ⊗_R M` vanish, and

`Tor_n^R(R ⧸ I, M) ≅ ⋀ⁿ(Rʳ) ⊗_R M`,

a direct sum of `r.choose n` copies of `M`. Hence `length_R Tor_n^R(R ⧸ I, M) = (r choose n) ·
length_R M`, these groups vanish for `n > r`, and the Euler characteristic
`∑ₙ (-1)ⁿ length_R Tor_n^R(R ⧸ I, M)` is `(1 - 1)ʳ · length_R M`, that is, `length_R M` if
`r = 0` and `0` otherwise.

The case of interest is a local ring `(R, 𝔪, κ)` and a sequence in `𝔪`, with `M = κ`: then
`Tor_n^R(R ⧸ I, κ)` is a `κ`-vector space of dimension `r.choose n`. When `R` is regular local
of dimension `c`, the maximal ideal is generated by a regular sequence of length `c`
([Stacks, Tag 00NQ]), so `Tor_n^R(κ, κ)` has length `c.choose n` and the alternating sum of
these lengths vanishes as soon as `c ≥ 1`.

## Main definitions

* `Koszul.homologySeqComplexTensorIsoOfLeAnnihilator`: if `(f₁, …, f_r)` kills `M`, the homology
  of `K_•(f) ⊗_R M` is its term `⋀ⁿ(Rʳ) ⊗_R M`.
* `Koszul.torIsoExteriorPowerTensorOfLeAnnihilator`: the identification
  `Tor_n^R(R ⧸ (f), M) ≅ ⋀ⁿ(Rʳ) ⊗_R M` for a Koszul-regular `f` and a module `M` killed by `(f)`.
* `Koszul.torSwapIsoExteriorPowerTensorOfLeAnnihilator`: the same with the two arguments of
  `Tor` exchanged.
* `Koszul.torResidueFieldIso`: `Torₙ^R(R ⧸ (f), κ) ≅ ⋀ⁿ(Rʳ) ⊗_R κ` for a local ring `(R, 𝔪, κ)`
  and a Koszul-regular sequence in `𝔪`.
* `IsLocalRing.quotientIsoResidueField`: `R ⧸ I ≅ κ` as `R`-modules when `I = 𝔪`.

## Main results

* `Module.length_tensorProduct_of_free`: `length_R (F ⊗_R M) = rank_R F · length_R M` for a
  finite free `R`-module `F`.
* `Koszul.length_tor_of_le_annihilator`: `length_R Tor_n^R(R ⧸ (f), M) = r.choose n · length_R M`.
* `Koszul.sum_range_neg_one_pow_mul_length_tor_of_le_annihilator`: the Euler characteristic
  `∑_{n ≤ r} (-1)ⁿ length_R Tor_n^R(R ⧸ (f), M)` is `length_R M` if `r = 0` and `0` otherwise.
* `Koszul.length_tor_residueField`, `Koszul.sum_range_neg_one_pow_mul_length_tor_residueField`:
  the case of the residue field of a local ring and a sequence in the maximal ideal.
* `IsRegularLocalRing.exists_isKoszulRegular_span_eq_maximalIdeal_of_ringKrullDim_eq`: the
  maximal ideal of a regular local ring of dimension `c` is generated by a Koszul-regular
  sequence of length `c`.
* `IsRegularLocalRing.length_tor_residueField_residueField`,
  `IsRegularLocalRing.isZero_tor_residueField_residueField_of_lt`,
  `IsRegularLocalRing.sum_range_neg_one_pow_mul_length_tor_residueField_residueField`: for a
  regular local ring of dimension `c`, `Tor_n^R(κ, κ)` has length `c.choose n`, vanishes for
  `n > c`, and the alternating sum of the lengths is `1` if `c = 0` and `0` otherwise.

## Implementation notes

`Tor` is Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Tor'`: `((Tor' (ModuleCat R) n).obj X).obj Y` is the `n`-th
left derived functor of `- ⊗_R Y` evaluated at `X`, which is the variable the Koszul resolution of
`R ⧸ (f)` resolves. The version with the arguments exchanged passes through the balancing
isomorphisms `Tor_iso_Tor'` and `torFlip_iso_Tor'` of Tag 00M1.

Lengths are `Module.length`, valued in `ℕ∞`; the Euler characteristics are integers, formed from
`ENat.toNat` of the lengths. The vanishing of `Tor_n` for `n > r` is
`Koszul.isZero_tor_of_lt`, so the sums over `Finset.range (r + 1)` are the full Euler
characteristics.

The hypothesis on the sequence is Koszul-regularity, which a regular sequence satisfies
(`Koszul.isKoszulRegularOn_and_isKoszulRegular_of_regular`); no Noetherian hypothesis is needed
for the computation itself.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0623](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0623)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 062F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/062F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00NQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00M1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00M1)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits IsLocalRing

open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

/-! ### Length of a tensor product with a finite free module -/

/-- **The length of `F ⊗_R M` for a finite free module `F`** is the rank of `F` times the length of
`M`: a basis of `F` identifies `F ⊗_R M` with a direct sum of `rank_R F` copies of `M`. -/
@[ega "IV 2.5.5.3" "special case"]
theorem Module.length_tensorProduct_of_free {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (F M : Type*)
    [AddCommGroup F] [Module R F] [Module.Free R F] [Module.Finite R F] [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module R M] :
    Module.length R (F ⊗[R] M) = Module.finrank R F * Module.length R M := by
  cases subsingleton_or_nontrivial R
  · simp [Module.length_eq_zero_of_subsingleton_ring]
  let b := Module.Free.chooseBasis R F
  rw [((b.repr.rTensor M).trans (TensorProduct.finsuppScalarLeft R M _)).length_eq,
    Module.length_finsupp, Module.finrank_eq_card_chooseBasisIndex,
    ENat.card_eq_coe_fintype_card]

namespace Koszul

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {r : ℕ}

/-! ### The Koszul complex with coefficients in a module killed by the sequence -/

/-- The Koszul differential of `f₁, …, f_r` dies after tensoring with a module `M` killed by
`(f₁, …, f_r)`: each of its coefficients lies in that ideal (`Koszul.d_seqDual_eq_sum_smul`). -/
theorem rTensor_d_eq_zero_of_le_annihilator (f : Fin r → R) {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module R M] (hM : Ideal.span (Set.range f) ≤ Module.annihilator R M) (n : ℕ) :
    LinearMap.rTensor M (d (seqDual f) n) = 0 := by
  refine TensorProduct.ext' fun x m => ?_
  have hm : ∀ k : Fin r, f k • m = 0 := fun k =>
    Module.mem_annihilator.1 (hM (Ideal.subset_span ⟨k, rfl⟩)) m
  rw [LinearMap.rTensor_tmul, LinearMap.zero_apply, d_seqDual_eq_sum_smul]
  simp only [LinearMap.sum_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply]
  rw [TensorProduct.sum_tmul]
  exact Finset.sum_eq_zero fun k _ => by
    rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul, hm k, TensorProduct.tmul_zero]

/-- The Koszul complex of `f₁, …, f_r` with coefficients in a module killed by
`(f₁, …, f_r)` has vanishing differentials. -/
theorem seqComplexTensor_d_eq_zero_of_le_annihilator (f : Fin r → R) (M : Type*)
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] (hM : Ideal.span (Set.range f) ≤ Module.annihilator R M)
    (i j : ℕ) : (seqComplexTensor f M).d i j = 0 := by
  by_cases hij : j + 1 = i
  · subst hij
    rw [seqComplexTensor_d, rTensor_d_eq_zero_of_le_annihilator f hM, ModuleCat.ofHom_zero]
    rfl
  · exact (seqComplexTensor f M).shape i j (by simpa using hij)

/-- If `(f₁, …, f_r)` kills `M`, the homology of `K_•(f₁, …, f_r) ⊗_R M` is its term
`⋀ⁿ(Rʳ) ⊗_R M`, the differentials being zero. -/
def homologySeqComplexTensorIsoOfLeAnnihilator (f : Fin r → R) (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module R M] (hM : Ideal.span (Set.range f) ≤ Module.annihilator R M) (n : ℕ) :
    (seqComplexTensor f M).homology n ≅ ModuleCat.of R ((⋀[R]^n (Fin r → R)) ⊗[R] M) :=
  (ShortComplex.LeftHomologyData.ofZeros ((seqComplexTensor f M).sc n)
    (seqComplexTensor_d_eq_zero_of_le_annihilator f M hM _ n)
    (seqComplexTensor_d_eq_zero_of_le_annihilator f M hM n _)).homologyIso

/-! ### `Tor` against a module killed by the sequence -/

/-- **`Tor` of a quotient by a Koszul-regular sequence against a module it kills.** For a
Koszul-regular sequence `f₁, …, f_r` and an `R`-module `M` annihilated by `(f₁, …, f_r)`,

`Torₙ^R(R ⧸ (f₁, …, f_r), M) ≅ ⋀ⁿ(Rʳ) ⊗_R M`. -/
def torIsoExteriorPowerTensorOfLeAnnihilator (f : Fin r → R) (hf : IsKoszulRegular f)
    (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    (hM : Ideal.span (Set.range f) ≤ Module.annihilator R M) (n : ℕ) :
    ((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj (ModuleCat.of R (R ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)))).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R M) ≅ ModuleCat.of R ((⋀[R]^n (Fin r → R)) ⊗[R] M) :=
  torIsoHomologySeqComplexTensor f hf M n ≪≫ homologySeqComplexTensorIsoOfLeAnnihilator f M hM n

/-- **The symmetric form of `Koszul.torIsoExteriorPowerTensorOfLeAnnihilator`.** For a
Koszul-regular sequence `f₁, …, f_r` and an `R`-module `M` annihilated by `(f₁, …, f_r)`,

`Torₙ^R(M, R ⧸ (f₁, …, f_r)) ≅ ⋀ⁿ(Rʳ) ⊗_R M`,

through the balancing isomorphisms of `Tor` (Tag 00M1). -/
def torSwapIsoExteriorPowerTensorOfLeAnnihilator (f : Fin r → R) (hf : IsKoszulRegular f)
    (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    (hM : Ideal.span (Set.range f) ≤ Module.annihilator R M) (n : ℕ) :
    ((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj (ModuleCat.of R M)).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R (R ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f))) ≅
      ModuleCat.of R ((⋀[R]^n (Fin r → R)) ⊗[R] M) :=
  ((torFlip_iso_Tor' R n).symm.app (ModuleCat.of R M)).app _ ≪≫
    ((Tor_iso_Tor' R n).app (ModuleCat.of R (R ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)))).app
      (ModuleCat.of R M) ≪≫
    torIsoExteriorPowerTensorOfLeAnnihilator f hf M hM n

/-- `⋀ⁿ(Rʳ) ⊗_R M` has length `r.choose n` times the length of `M`, since `⋀ⁿ(Rʳ)` is free of
rank `r.choose n`. -/
theorem length_exteriorPower_tensor (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] (n : ℕ) :
    Module.length R ((⋀[R]^n (Fin r → R)) ⊗[R] M) = r.choose n * Module.length R M := by
  cases subsingleton_or_nontrivial R
  · simp [Module.length_eq_zero_of_subsingleton_ring]
  rw [Module.length_tensorProduct_of_free, exteriorPower.finrank_eq, Module.finrank_fin_fun]

/-- **The length of `Tor` against a module killed by a Koszul-regular sequence.** For a
Koszul-regular sequence `f₁, …, f_r` and an `R`-module `M` annihilated by `(f₁, …, f_r)`,

`length_R Torₙ^R(R ⧸ (f₁, …, f_r), M) = (r choose n) · length_R M`. -/
theorem length_tor_of_le_annihilator (f : Fin r → R) (hf : IsKoszulRegular f)
    (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    (hM : Ideal.span (Set.range f) ≤ Module.annihilator R M) (n : ℕ) :
    Module.length R (((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R (R ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)))).obj (ModuleCat.of R M)) =
      r.choose n * Module.length R M := by
  rw [(torIsoExteriorPowerTensorOfLeAnnihilator f hf M hM n).toLinearEquiv.length_eq,
    length_exteriorPower_tensor]

/-- The symmetric form of `Koszul.length_tor_of_le_annihilator`:
`length_R Torₙ^R(M, R ⧸ (f₁, …, f_r)) = (r choose n) · length_R M`. -/
theorem length_tor_swap_of_le_annihilator (f : Fin r → R) (hf : IsKoszulRegular f)
    (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    (hM : Ideal.span (Set.range f) ≤ Module.annihilator R M) (n : ℕ) :
    Module.length R (((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj (ModuleCat.of R M)).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R (R ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)))) =
      r.choose n * Module.length R M := by
  rw [(torSwapIsoExteriorPowerTensorOfLeAnnihilator f hf M hM n).toLinearEquiv.length_eq,
    length_exteriorPower_tensor]

/-- The alternating sum `∑_{n ≤ r} (-1)ⁿ (r choose n) · ℓ` is `ℓ` if `r = 0` and `0` otherwise. -/
theorem sum_range_neg_one_pow_mul_toNat_choose_mul (ℓ : ℕ∞) :
    ∑ n ∈ Finset.range (r + 1), (-1 : ℤ) ^ n * (((r.choose n : ℕ∞) * ℓ).toNat : ℤ) =
      if r = 0 then (ℓ.toNat : ℤ) else 0 := by
  simp only [ENat.toNat_mul, ENat.toNat_natCast, Nat.cast_mul, ← mul_assoc, ← Finset.sum_mul,
    Int.alternating_sum_range_choose, ite_mul, one_mul, zero_mul]

/-- **The Euler characteristic of `Tor` against a module killed by a Koszul-regular sequence.**
For a Koszul-regular sequence `f₁, …, f_r` and an `R`-module `M` annihilated by `(f₁, …, f_r)`,

`∑_{n ≤ r} (-1)ⁿ length_R Torₙ^R(R ⧸ (f₁, …, f_r), M) = (1 - 1)ʳ · length_R M`,

that is, `length_R M` if `r = 0` and `0` otherwise. The groups `Torₙ` with `n > r` vanish
(`Koszul.isZero_tor_of_lt`), so this is the whole Euler characteristic. -/
theorem sum_range_neg_one_pow_mul_length_tor_of_le_annihilator (f : Fin r → R)
    (hf : IsKoszulRegular f) (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    (hM : Ideal.span (Set.range f) ≤ Module.annihilator R M) :
    ∑ n ∈ Finset.range (r + 1), (-1 : ℤ) ^ n * ((Module.length R (((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R (R ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)))).obj (ModuleCat.of R M))).toNat : ℤ) =
      if r = 0 then ((Module.length R M).toNat : ℤ) else 0 := by
  simp only [length_tor_of_le_annihilator f hf M hM]
  exact sum_range_neg_one_pow_mul_toNat_choose_mul _

/-! ### The residue field of a local ring -/

/-- An ideal generated by elements of the maximal ideal annihilates the residue field. -/
theorem span_le_annihilator_residueField [IsLocalRing R] (f : Fin r → R)
    (hfm : ∀ k, f k ∈ maximalIdeal R) :
    Ideal.span (Set.range f) ≤ Module.annihilator R (ResidueField R) :=
  Ideal.span_le.2 <| by
    rintro _ ⟨k, rfl⟩
    exact Module.mem_annihilator.2 fun c => Stacks.OrderOfVanishing.smul_residueField_eq_zero
      (hfm k) c

/-- **`Tor` of a quotient by a Koszul-regular sequence in the maximal ideal against the residue
field.** For a local ring `(R, 𝔪, κ)` and a Koszul-regular sequence `f₁, …, f_r ∈ 𝔪`,

`Torₙ^R(R ⧸ (f₁, …, f_r), κ) ≅ ⋀ⁿ(Rʳ) ⊗_R κ`,

a `κ`-vector space of dimension `r.choose n`. -/
def torResidueFieldIso [IsLocalRing R] (f : Fin r → R) (hf : IsKoszulRegular f)
    (hfm : ∀ k, f k ∈ maximalIdeal R) (n : ℕ) :
    ((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj (ModuleCat.of R (R ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)))).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R)) ≅
      ModuleCat.of R ((⋀[R]^n (Fin r → R)) ⊗[R] ResidueField R) :=
  torIsoExteriorPowerTensorOfLeAnnihilator f hf (ResidueField R)
    (span_le_annihilator_residueField f hfm) n

/-- **The length of `Tor` against the residue field.** For a local ring `(R, 𝔪, κ)` and a
Koszul-regular sequence `f₁, …, f_r ∈ 𝔪`,

`length_R Torₙ^R(R ⧸ (f₁, …, f_r), κ) = r choose n`;

in particular it vanishes for `n > r`. -/
theorem length_tor_residueField [IsLocalRing R] (f : Fin r → R) (hf : IsKoszulRegular f)
    (hfm : ∀ k, f k ∈ maximalIdeal R) (n : ℕ) :
    Module.length R (((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R (R ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)))).obj
          (ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R))) = r.choose n := by
  rw [length_tor_of_le_annihilator f hf _ (span_le_annihilator_residueField f hfm),
    Stacks.OrderOfVanishing.length_residueField, mul_one]

/-- The symmetric form of `Koszul.length_tor_residueField`:
`length_R Torₙ^R(κ, R ⧸ (f₁, …, f_r)) = r choose n`. -/
theorem length_tor_swap_residueField [IsLocalRing R] (f : Fin r → R) (hf : IsKoszulRegular f)
    (hfm : ∀ k, f k ∈ maximalIdeal R) (n : ℕ) :
    Module.length R (((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj (ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R))).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R (R ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)))) = r.choose n := by
  rw [length_tor_swap_of_le_annihilator f hf _ (span_le_annihilator_residueField f hfm),
    Stacks.OrderOfVanishing.length_residueField, mul_one]

/-- **The Euler characteristic of `Tor` against the residue field.** For a local ring
`(R, 𝔪, κ)` and a Koszul-regular sequence `f₁, …, f_r ∈ 𝔪`,

`∑_{n ≤ r} (-1)ⁿ length_R Torₙ^R(R ⧸ (f₁, …, f_r), κ) = (1 - 1)ʳ`,

which is `1` if `r = 0` and `0` if `r ≥ 1`. -/
theorem sum_range_neg_one_pow_mul_length_tor_residueField [IsLocalRing R] (f : Fin r → R)
    (hf : IsKoszulRegular f) (hfm : ∀ k, f k ∈ maximalIdeal R) :
    ∑ n ∈ Finset.range (r + 1), (-1 : ℤ) ^ n * ((Module.length R (((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R (R ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)))).obj
          (ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R)))).toNat : ℤ) =
      if r = 0 then 1 else 0 := by
  rw [sum_range_neg_one_pow_mul_length_tor_of_le_annihilator f hf _
    (span_le_annihilator_residueField f hfm), Stacks.OrderOfVanishing.length_residueField]
  simp

end Koszul

/-! ### Regular local rings -/

/-- The quotient of a local ring by an ideal equal to its maximal ideal is the residue field, as
an `R`-module. -/
def IsLocalRing.quotientIsoResidueField {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] {I : Ideal R}
    (hI : I = maximalIdeal R) :
    ModuleCat.of R (R ⧸ I) ≅ ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R) :=
  (Submodule.quotEquivOfEq _ _ hI).toModuleIso

namespace IsRegularLocalRing

open Koszul

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsRegularLocalRing R]

/-- **The maximal ideal of a regular local ring of dimension `c` is generated by a Koszul-regular
sequence of length `c`.** A minimal generating family of the maximal ideal has `c` elements and is
a regular sequence ([Stacks, Tag 00NQ]), hence Koszul-regular. -/
theorem exists_isKoszulRegular_span_eq_maximalIdeal_of_ringKrullDim_eq {c : ℕ}
    (hc : ringKrullDim R = c) :
    ∃ x : Fin c → R, Ideal.span (Set.range x) = maximalIdeal R ∧ IsKoszulRegular x := by
  obtain ⟨s, hcard, hspan⟩ :=
    (IsNoetherian.noetherian (maximalIdeal R)).exists_span_finset_card_eq_spanFinrank
  have hgen : Ideal.ofList s.toList = maximalIdeal R := by
    rw [← hspan]
    simp [Ideal.ofList]
  have hlen : s.toList.length = (maximalIdeal R).spanFinrank := by simp [hcard]
  have hreg : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R s.toList :=
    (isRegular_and_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_and_isMaximalCohenMacaulay R).1 s.toList hgen
      hlen |>.1
  have hc' : s.toList.length = c := by
    have h := (IsRegularLocalRing.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal (R := R)).trans hc
    rw [hlen]
    exact_mod_cast h
  subst hc'
  refine ⟨s.toList.get, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [show Set.range s.toList.get = {y | y ∈ s.toList} from by
      ext y
      exact List.mem_iff_get.symm]
    exact hgen
  · refine (isKoszulRegularOn_and_isKoszulRegular_of_regular (M := R)).2.2 ?_
    rwa [List.ofFn_get s.toList]

/-- `Tor_n^R(R ⧸ I, κ) ≅ Tor_n^R(κ, κ)` when `I` is the maximal ideal. -/
private def torQuotientResidueFieldIso {I : Ideal R} (hI : I = maximalIdeal R) (n : ℕ) :
    ((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj (ModuleCat.of R (R ⧸ I))).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R)) ≅
      ((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj (ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R))).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R)) :=
  ((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).mapIso (quotientIsoResidueField hI)).app _

/-- **The length of `Tor_n^R(κ, κ)` for a regular local ring.** If `R` is a regular local ring of
dimension `c` with residue field `κ`, then `length_R Torₙ^R(κ, κ) = c choose n`. -/
@[ega "III 7.6.11" "partial"]
theorem length_tor_residueField_residueField {c : ℕ} (hc : ringKrullDim R = c) (n : ℕ) :
    Module.length R (((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj (ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R))).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R))) = c.choose n := by
  obtain ⟨x, hx, hreg⟩ := exists_isKoszulRegular_span_eq_maximalIdeal_of_ringKrullDim_eq hc
  have hfm : ∀ k, x k ∈ maximalIdeal R := fun k => hx ▸ Ideal.subset_span ⟨k, rfl⟩
  rw [(torQuotientResidueFieldIso hx n).toLinearEquiv.symm.length_eq]
  exact length_tor_residueField x hreg hfm n

/-- For a regular local ring `R` of dimension `c` with residue field `κ`, `Torₙ^R(κ, κ) = 0` for
`n > c`. -/
theorem isZero_tor_residueField_residueField_of_lt {c : ℕ} (hc : ringKrullDim R = c) {n : ℕ}
    (hn : c < n) :
    IsZero (((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj (ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R))).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R))) := by
  obtain ⟨x, hx, hreg⟩ := exists_isKoszulRegular_span_eq_maximalIdeal_of_ringKrullDim_eq hc
  exact (isZero_tor_of_lt x hreg (ResidueField R) hn).of_iso
    (torQuotientResidueFieldIso hx n).symm

/-- **The Euler characteristic of `Tor^R(κ, κ)` for a regular local ring.** If `R` is a regular
local ring of dimension `c` with residue field `κ`, then

`∑_{n ≤ c} (-1)ⁿ length_R Torₙ^R(κ, κ) = (1 - 1)ᶜ`,

which is `1` if `c = 0` and `0` if `c ≥ 1`. The groups `Torₙ` with `n > c` vanish
(`IsRegularLocalRing.isZero_tor_residueField_residueField_of_lt`). -/
theorem sum_range_neg_one_pow_mul_length_tor_residueField_residueField {c : ℕ}
    (hc : ringKrullDim R = c) :
    ∑ n ∈ Finset.range (c + 1), (-1 : ℤ) ^ n * ((Module.length R (((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} R) n).obj
        (ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R))).obj (ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R)))).toNat : ℤ) =
      if c = 0 then 1 else 0 := by
  simp only [length_tor_residueField_residueField hc, ENat.toNat_natCast]
  exact Int.alternating_sum_range_choose

end IsRegularLocalRing

